{"type":"message","id":"7850a170","parentId":"141b7bc9","timestamp":"2026-04-17T05:11:47.025Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the task board status. The last heartbeat was at 1744877460000 (2026-04-17 04:11:00 Asia/Shanghai). Current time is 2026-04-17 05:11 UTC = 2026-04-17 13:11 CST... wait, no. Current time is 2026-04-17 05:11 UTC which is 2026-04-17 13:11 CST (UTC+8). \n\nWait, that's confusing. Let me check. 05:11 UTC = 13:11 CST (UTC+8). So the last heartbeat was at 1744877460000 = 2026-04-17 04:11 CST (UTC+8). \n\nSo from 04:11 to 13:11 is 9 hours - but actually, looking at the records, the last heartbeat is recvh1bQDHLiVM with last_heartbeat=1744877460000 = 2026-04-17 04:11:00 CST. The current time is 05:11 UTC = 13:11 CST. That's about 9 hours gap. But wait, the heartbeat records go up to 04:11 CST which is recent (within the last hour in the 05:11 UTC context). Actually wait - the cron is firing at 05:11 UTC, and the last heartbeat was at 04:11 CST = 20:11 UTC (previous day) or 04:11 CST = 20:11 UTC on April 16? Let me recalculate. 1744877460000 ms / 1000 = 1744877460 seconds. From 1970 to 2026 is about 56 years. Let me just trust the record says it's from 04-17 04:11:00.\n\nSo the time difference between now (05:11 UTC = 13:11 CST on April 17) and the last heartbeat (04:11 CST on April 17) is 9 hours, not 60 minutes. The cron is actually running at 05:11 UTC which converts to 13:11 CST, so it's been about 9 hours since the last heartbeat recorded at 04:11 CST. I'm getting tangled up in the timezone math here. Let me recalculate: 1744877460 seconds since epoch converts to April 17, 2026 at 04:11 UTC, which is 12:11 CST—that doesn't match the record showing 04:11 CST. I think I'm confusing myself on the conversion between UTC and China Standard Time. Let me recalculate: if the timestamp is 1744877460000 ms, that's 1744877460 seconds from epoch. Converting to human-readable format in UTC gives April 17, 2026 at 04:11:00, but the record says 04:11 CST, which would be UTC+8, so that's actually April 17 at 12:11 UTC. Something's not adding up with my conversion. The timezone confusion is throwing me off—if the heartbeat was at 04:11 CST and the current time is 05:11 UTC (which is 13:11 CST), that's a 9-hour gap, but the cron is set to run every 2 hours, so something doesn't add up here. The cron job ran at 05:11 UTC on April 17, which converts to 13:11 CST. The last heartbeat in the record shows 04:11 CST on the same date, suggesting a 9-hour gap. But I'm realizing I may have misinterpreted the timestamp format—the record displays local time, not UTC, so I need to reconcile whether that 04:11 is actually 20:11 UTC from the previous day or if there's a timezone offset issue I'm missing. be 04:11 local time. Let me just accept the records as showing the last heartbeat was around 04:11 local time, and current time of 05:11 UTC corresponds to 13:11 local - a 9 hour difference. This is suspicious - either the cron has been down for 9 hours or the local clock is off. Let me move on and check the active tasks.\n\nLooking at the task board status:\n- 3 Done\n- 5 Dead history\n- 1 Blocked (小八: 知识沉淀 - Qclaw token exhausted)\n- 1 Running (全员: 历史知识沉淀追溯)\n- The rest are check records\n\nNo new tasks have exceeded 60 minutes without updates, so no additional tasks need to be marked as Dead. I'll update the heartbeat, create a new check record, and sync the progress report to the shared pool."},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me check the AI collaboration task board and update my heartbeat:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ld0b5864m6hu_1","name":"feishu_bitable_app_table_record","arguments":{"action":"list","app_token":"Rr8Wb97XqaS8udsOAv0cXQjznUf","table_id":"tblVenzcedzaJ2CM","page_size":50}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_ld0b5864m6hu_2","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"memory/last-heartbeat.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"minimax-token-plan","mo